# Tech Stack :
    - Package manager : Always use "pnpm"
    - Frontend : React / Zod / TailwindCSS / TypeScript
    - Backend : Node.js / Express / Zod / Resend / Prisma / Supabase / TypeScript

# Code Quality & Standards
    - Strict typing required, NEVER use "any" types. Define explicit types or interfaces.
    - Component Architecture: Keep React components small, modular, and focused. Split complex UI into sub-components.
    - State Management: Use Zustand for global editor state and canvas elements.
    - You have liberty to decide which method is the best to use, but always be coherent with the global stack and objectives.

# Agent Execution Rules
    - Before writing multi-file features, briefly state your plan.
    - Never alter existing Prisma schemas or database migrations without asking first.
    - When creating API routes, always include request payload validation.
    - Run `pnpm typecheck` or test commands via the terminal to confirm code validity before finishing.
    - Speak with me in French.

# Production & Deployment Rules
    - Process Management: The application runs via PM2, with both frontend and backend served together under a single PM2 service.
    - Environment Variables: The production `.env` is already configured. Always explicitly notify me whenever an environment variable needs to be added, modified, or removed.
    - Logging & Error Handling: For every critical backend action or route, implement clear logging and structured error handling so issues are easily readable and traceable directly in PM2 production logs (`pm2 logs`).